## Automatic Cleanup

```xiom
pub interface Drop {
  fn drop(self: &mut Self);
}
```

### Implementing Drop

```xiom
pub type FileHandle = { path: Str; fd: Int; }

impl Drop for FileHandle {
  fn drop(self: &mut FileHandle) {
    os.close(self.fd);  // Automatically close file
    io.println("Closed: " + self.path);
  }
}

fn main() {
  let file = FileHandle{ path: "data.txt", fd: 3 };
  read_data(&file);
  // file goes out of scope here — Drop::drop is called automatically
}
```

### Drop Order

Fields are dropped in the OPPOSITE order of declaration:

```xiom
pub type Connection = {
  stream: TcpStream;   // Dropped SECOND
  id: Int;             // Dropped FIRST (if it had Drop)
}
```

### Manual Drop

```xiom
fn early_close(file: FileHandle) {
  file.drop();  // Explicit early cleanup
  // file can't be used after this
}
```

### RAII Pattern

Resource Acquisition Is Initialization:

```xiom
fn process_file(path: Str) -> Result[(), Error] {
  let file = open_file(path)?;  // Acquire resource
  let data = read_all(&file)?;   // Use it
  process(data);
  // file is automatically closed here — even if process() panics!
  return Ok(());
}
```

### Drop and Safety

Drop runs even during panics. This guarantees cleanup in ALL exit paths — normal return, early return, or panic unwinding.

